humbnail":""},{"id":"1775581969752","neuronKeys":["[#3fa6f]","[#e4ef2]","[#436e2]","[#ee353]","[#32402]","[#72a6c]","[#f26c8]","[#ae7af]"],"edgeStrings":["[#ae7af]_#_[#3fa6f]","[#3fa6f]_#_[#d27de]","[#e4ef2]_#_[#436e2]","[#436e2]_#_[#203d5]","[#32402]_#_[#cd80b]","[#ee353]_#_[#32402]","[#72a6c]_#_[#f26c8]","[#f26c8]_#_[#b2670]"],"description":"We also send another stronger signal to control each motor with joystick inputs, but normally, these will not be allowed to spike.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775582030842","neuronKeys":["[#774a8]","[#3fa6f]","[#436e2]","[#32402]","[#f26c8]"],"edgeStrings":["[#774a8]_#_[#3fa6f]","[#774a8]_#_[#f26c8]","[#774a8]_#_[#32402]","[#774a8]_#_[#436e2]"],"description":"This central inhibitory neuron is set to be highly active. It spikes all the time without any input, and by default, it wants to silence the high speed neuronswhen we try to trigger them.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775582109474","neuronKeys":["[#56686]","[#774a8]","[#3fa6f]","[#436e2]","[#32402]","[#f26c8]"],"edgeStrings":["[#56686]_#_[#774a8]"],"description":"If we pull the right trigger on the game controller, we will stop the highly active inhibitory neuron from spiking. Now, the 4 high speed motor neurons can fire when we push the joystick, as long as we keep R2 held down!","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775582163547","neuronKeys":["[#73332]","[#1b413]"],"edgeStrings":["[#73332]_#_[#0c482]","[#73332]_#_[#80e1a]","[#1b413]_#_[#73332]"],"description":"We have a similar setup, using the left trigger on our controller, and another highly active inhibitory neuron. What behavior will activate when we hold down L2?","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775582306786","neuronKeys":["[#80e1a]","[#0c482]"],"edgeStrings":["[#5bb2b]_#_[#80e1a]","[#80e1a]_#_[#d27de]","[#5bb2b]_#_[#0c482]","[#0c482]_#_[#b2670]"],"description":"When we hold L2, we allow Spikerbot to track a person! The neuron on the Left will drive Spikerbot automatically to the right whenever a person is seen on SpikerBot’s right side, and the opposite neuron will drive SpikerBot to the left when a person is on our Left. This is a classic Braitenberg Vehicle, enabled on demand!","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775582470994","neuronKeys":["[#19c16]","[#27cec]","[#2ca0b]","[#b5f7c]"],"edgeStrings":["[#19c16]_#_[#27cec]","[#19c16]_#_[#2ca0b]","[#27cec]_#_[#2ca0b]","[#2ca0b]_#_[#bcb0e]","[#19c16]_#_[#b5f7c]","[#b5f7c]_#_[#1fb03]"],"description":"When we press the ‘a’ button on our gamepad, we can trigger a sound effect with simple Feed Forward Inhibition. Each time we press the ‘a’ button, we will trigger lights, and a sound effect will play just once.","thumbnail":""}],"info":{"title":"Two Speed Tank ","description":"Drives each wheel seperate like a tank at two different speeds with your gamepad!","author":"User","version":"1.0.1","timestamp":"2026-04-07T13:21:15.580494"}}